  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "gale-sentinel",
      "id": "LUG-07",
      "plano": "gale-sentinel",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.zSkwEUUtkNGhfXun]{Gale Sentinel Campus and Data Center}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.5hwXPdn0tUJ3NaKZ.JournalEntryPage.wIpc0OR2nQf7WDFO]{A1-E05 · The City's Eyes} · @UUID[JournalEntry.C7cxKf7kcAELzuJ1.JournalEntryPage.EjJ0vfVBCjTTb0QV]{A3-E02 · The Data Center}</p>\n<p><strong>Layer 1 of A3-E02: the perimeter.</strong> “Two a.m. The Gale Sentinel lobby is empty except for a guard looking at his phone behind the desk. The wall screen is still on: a mosaic of thousands of live feeds, porches, hallways, rain.” The <strong>video wall</strong> takes up the north wall of the lobby, facing the main entrance; on the map it&#39;s off, and three “video wall” lights turn it on. Beneath it runs the motto “We see what the city doesn&#39;t.” (it isn&#39;t painted: no text on the map). The guard (one of the <strong>two mortal guards</strong>) sits in the chair behind the <strong>reception desk</strong>; the other is in the <strong>security office</strong> in the west wing, with the camera monitors.</p>\n<p><strong>ANOMALY cameras (at every entrance)</strong>, marked as <code>anomaly</code> objects with no light: ① above the main entrance, outside; ② in the southeast corner of the lobby, aimed at the door; ③ above the service exit to the yard, outside; ④ in the elevator hall, aimed at the turnstiles. Every Kindred who passes in front of one with the module active is logged as a “cold subject”: Thermometer +1 in total (A3-E02, layer 1). Disabling it from outside: Intelligence + Technology Diff. 4 (Ezra +2 dice if he already knows the firmware is his; LOR-03 at level 4: automatic). Obfuscate doesn&#39;t fool it.</p>\n<p><strong>Entrances.</strong> The main entrance (sliding glass door) opens onto the plaza and the parking lot: the “To the campus parking lot” region leads to the campus zone map (pending, t2i). The <strong>service exit</strong> off the north hallway opens onto the service yard, and from the yard you cross to the <strong>data center</strong> (region → <code>gale-datos</code>). The <strong>turnstiles</strong> (two card-access lanes, glass gates between railings) separate the lobby from the elevator hall; the service hallway also reaches the hall through a door with an electronic lock. Stairs and elevators go up to the <strong>third floor</strong> (<code>gale-planta3</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>A1-E05 (physical access).</strong> If the coterie uses Dominate on an on-call technician to get in, they come in this way and pass camera ① or ③: Thermometer +1 unless the cameras are disabled first.</p>\n<p><strong>Running out</strong> through the lobby and the plaza in front of the cameras: Thermometer +1. If the alarm goes off, Bellevue police take twelve minutes.</p>\n<p>The ground-floor café and restrooms (hatched block to the southeast) are closed and aren&#39;t played.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (5) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> To the campus parking lot.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
